posts.body:
@AquaEcho
good info/data! But what happened with MZ? I see that many folks have concluded that the improvements aren't worth upgrading from MV.
I personally love my RPG Maker MV. It's an engine with a lot of potential!

@AquaEcho
Good writing! Why don't they think and plan long, take a risk, and work hard to create a good RM?
Where is Yoji Ojima now? 6 years without a new RPG Maker is a new record and is quite long.

I personally would love more single-genre makers, like the ones
@Akkari
has mentioned here! I would buy them!

@AquaEcho
Thank you for this informative answer, sir!
Also, I wonder... What can be done about the heavy reliance on 3rd party plugins? I wonder if they can perhaps create a better system than plugins. Is this even possible?

@AquaEcho
You really know it and are really good at this analysis, sir!
This seems like a potentially exciting feature, or at least interesting to watch unfold.
